kind: vulnerability
title: "Microsoft Semantic Kernel: prompt injection to code execution in the Python SDK (CVE-2026-26030) and host file write in the .NET SDK (CVE-2026-25592)"
headline: "Two Semantic Kernel flaws let a prompt-injected agent run code or write files on the host; fixed in 1.39.4 and 1.71.0"
summary: "Microsoft's Defender research team described on 2026-05-07 two Semantic Kernel flaws disclosed in February, each CVSS 9.9. CVE-2026-26030 lets model-controlled input reach an eval() in the Python SDK's in-memory vector store filter (fixed in 1.39.4); CVE-2026-25592 let a model call a .NET SDK function that writes files to any host path, such as the Windows Startup folder (fixed in 1.71.0). Both need a prompt-injection path into an agent that uses the affected component; neither is reported exploited."
